Mon Aug 31 07:36:06 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 5.7.0
  * Integrated latest RTL-SDR adaptation from @old-dab to support
    RTL-SDR Blog V4L.
  * Added traffic light status icons with distinct color states
    (green, yellow-green, yellow, red-yellow, red, orange, off).
  * Added SNR and MER display on the main window (use the A/Q toggle
    button to switch between audio level and SNR/MER bar graphs).
  * Modularized audio processing and playback into a dedicated
    AudioPipeline class for cleaner threading.
  * Accelerated frequency correction calculation using VOLK SIMD
    kernels.
  * Improved fine frequency correction precision.
  * Fixed a brief UI freeze when rendering "PRS Phase unwrapped".
  * Reworked sub-window opening and closing behavior; toggle buttons
    now feature a small yellow indicator showing the window's open
    state.
  * Fixed an issue in the TII web server when handling empty TII
    content (untested under real-world conditions).
  * Various internal optimizations and code cleanups.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Aug  8 14:49:44 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 5.6.0
  RTL-TCP Client Rework
  * The RTL-TCP client was refactored in depth. Connection handling
    is now stable and self-reporting.
    + The device window got a new layout. It shows a clear
      connection state.
    + One Connect / Disconnect toggle button replaces the two
      former buttons.
    + The address field accepts host or host:port. Without a port,
      1234 is used.
    + Pressing Return after entering the address is no longer
      necessary.
    + A lost connection is detected and reported. Formerly the
      reader stayed silently "connected".
    + Socket errors are logged. The tuner type display is reset on
      disconnect.
    + Input ring buffer overflows are detected and logged. Dropped
      sample counts are reported.
    + An odd byte count from the server is flagged, as it would
      silently destroy the I/Q alignment.
    + The channel restarts itself as soon as the server connection
      is established. The connection may come up long after the
      device was created.
   Reception Robustness
   * The tuner settle time after a (re-)tune no longer blocks the
     GUI thread. Samples are discarded sample-wise in the processor
     thread instead. Devices that read in the GUI thread (rtl_tcp)
     delivered nothing during the former sleep.
   * The FIB decoder now validates the sub-channel organization
     (FIG 0/1). A sub-channel may not exceed the 864 CUs of a CIF
     and may not overlap another one.
   * If an impossible content is found, the whole collected FIB
     data is discarded and the collection restarts. This removes
     corrupted ensemble data caused by stale samples at channel
     start.
   * FIB decoder timers are no longer touched across thread
     boundaries.
   TII Database
   * The TII handler now supports multiple channels per ensemble.
     One ensemble (EId) can be transmitted on several channels,
     e.g. regional windows of a nationwide multiplex.
   * The lookup first tries the current channel. It falls back to
     the first matching EId/TII entry otherwise.
   * Channel mismatch warnings are reported only once per key. The
     log is no longer flooded.
   * Ignored tunnel entries are counted in the load statistics.
   Removed Devices
   * The following unmaintained device handlers were removed:
     + Elad S1
     + Colibri
     + ExtIO

